---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /en/savings-calculator/index.html
title: Savings calculator
pageScript: /assets/js/calculator.js
description: >-
  Estimate what your ward loses around unspecific nurse calls each year. Runs entirely in your
  browser — no sign-up, no email required, nothing sent to us.
---
{% macro field(key, label, hint, suffix) %}
  {% set limit = calculator.limits[key] %}
  <div class="field">
    <div class="field__top">
      <label for="f-{{ key }}">{{ label }}</label>
      <span class="field__value" data-out="{{ key }}Value"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="field__row">
      <input
        type="range"
        id="f-{{ key }}"
        data-range="{{ key }}"
        min="{{ limit.min }}"
        max="{{ limit.max }}"
        step="{{ limit.step }}"
        value="{{ calculator.defaults[key] }}"
        aria-describedby="h-{{ key }}"
      />
      <input
        type="number"
        data-number="{{ key }}"
        min="{{ limit.min }}"
        max="{{ limit.max }}"
        step="{{ limit.step }}"
        value="{{ calculator.defaults[key] }}"
        aria-label="{{ label }} ({{ suffix }})"
      />
    </div>
    <p class="field__hint" id="h-{{ key }}">{{ hint }}</p>
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Savings calculator</p>
    <h1>What do unspecific calls cost you a year?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Not a lead-capture form. Move the sliders and the numbers move with them. Everything runs in
      your browser: no account, no email needed to see the result, and nothing is sent to us.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="shell" id="calculator" data-lang="{{ lang }}">
    <script type="application/json" id="calculator-config">{{ calculator | dump | safe }}</script>

    <div class="calc">
      <div class="calc__panel">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem">Your ward</h2>

        <div class="calc__presets" role="group" aria-label="Starting points">
          {% for preset in calculator.presets %}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="calc__preset"
              data-preset-beds="{{ preset.beds }}"
              aria-pressed="false"
            >{{ preset.label[lang] }} · {{ preset.beds }} beds</button>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {{ field("beds", "Beds", "How many beds the estimate covers.", "beds") }}
        {{ field("occupancy", "Average occupancy", "Share of those beds occupied across the year.", "percent") }}
        {{ field("callsPerPatientDay", "Nurse calls per patient-day", "Swiss hospital statistics put this at roughly 8.", "calls") }}
        {{ field("wastedMinutesPerCall", "Minutes lost per call", "Walking back for equipment, finding a qualified colleague, checking an accidental call.", "minutes") }}
        {{ field("nursingCostPerHour", "Nursing cost per hour (CHF)", "Fully loaded cost of an hour of nursing time, including employer costs.", "CHF per hour") }}

        <hr />

        {{ field("patonCostPerBedPerYear", "Indicative PATON cost per bed per year (CHF)", "Indicative only — not a quote. Set it to zero to see the gross figure alone.", "CHF per bed per year") }}
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="calc__result" aria-live="polite">
          <dl class="calc__headline">
            <dt>Value of nursing time currently lost, per year</dt>
            <dd data-out="annualSaving">—</dd>
          </dl>

          <dl class="calc__breakdown">
            <div>
              <dt>Nurse calls a year</dt>
              <dd data-out="calls">—</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Occupied bed-days</dt>
              <dd data-out="bedDays">—</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Nursing hours lost</dt>
              <dd data-out="hoursLost">—</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <div class="calc__compare">
            <p class="eyebrow" style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; color: var(--orange)">Your cost vs our price</p>
            <div class="calc__compare-row">
              <span>Time you are losing today</span>
              <span data-out="grossSaving">—</span>
            </div>
            <div class="calc__compare-row">
              <span>Indicative PATON cost</span>
              <span data-out="patonCost">—</span>
            </div>
            <div class="calc__compare-row calc__compare-row--total">
              <span>Net benefit a year</span>
              <span data-out="netBenefit">—</span>
            </div>
            <div class="calc__compare-row">
              <span>Value returned per franc spent</span>
              <span data-out="ratio">—</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          {#
            Capacity framing, kept deliberately soft. This is minutes handed back to the ward —
            it is NEVER to be expressed as full-time equivalents or as a headcount reduction.
            Nursing is short-staffed; selling redundancies here would be both wrong and untrue.
          #}
          <p class="calc__capacity">
            That is roughly <strong data-out="minutesPerBedPerDay">—</strong> of nursing time handed
            back to the ward, per bed, per day. We report it as time returned to the team, never as
            a headcount you could cut.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="calc__share">
          <h3>Want a copy?</h3>
          <p class="note" style="margin-bottom: 1rem">
            Optional. This opens your own email app with the figures already written out. No form is
            submitted, no address reaches us, and nothing is stored anywhere.
          </p>
          <form class="calc__share-form" data-share-form novalidate>
            <label class="visually-hidden" for="share-email">Your email address</label>
            <input
              type="email"
              id="share-email"
              name="email"
              placeholder="you@clinic.ch"
              autocomplete="email"
            />
            <button class="button" type="submit">Email me this summary</button>
          </form>
          <p class="calc__status" data-share-status role="status"></p>
        </div>

        <details class="calc__assumptions">
          <summary>How the number is worked out</summary>
          <div class="prose" style="padding-top: 0.5rem">
            <p>Four multiplications, all of them visible as inputs above:</p>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Occupied bed-days</strong> = beds × occupancy × 365</li>
              <li><strong>Nurse calls</strong> = occupied bed-days × calls per patient-day</li>
              <li><strong>Minutes lost</strong> = nurse calls × minutes lost per call</li>
              <li><strong>Value</strong> = minutes lost ÷ 60 × nursing cost per hour</li>
            </ol>
            <p>
              The baseline assumptions — around 8 calls per patient-day and around 2.5 minutes lost
              per call — come from Swiss federal hospital statistics together with PATON's own
              observation work on wards. They are averages: your ward will differ, which is exactly
              why every one of them is an input rather than a constant.
            </p>
            <p>
              The PATON cost figure is indicative and is there so the comparison is honest. It is
              not a quote. <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=PATON%20—%20pricing">Ask us for a real one.</a>
            </p>
            <p class="note">
              This is a model of avoidable time, not a promise of cash released. Treat it the way
              you would treat any business case: a starting point for a conversation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <noscript>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top: 2rem">
        The calculator needs JavaScript to recalculate. The formula is written out above, and we are
        happy to run it with you by email: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.
      </p>
    </noscript>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="cta">
      <div>
        <h2>Does the number look plausible?</h2>
        <p>
          Send us your inputs and we will tell you where we think the model is optimistic and where
          it is conservative for a ward like yours.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button button--light" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=PATON%20—%20savings%20model">
          {{ site.email }}
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
